{"name":"Sail Away","hex":"#55b4de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of fabric attached to a boat and arranged such that it causes the wind to drive the boat along. The sail may be attached to the boat via a combination of mast, spars and ropes.","The concept of a sail or sails, as if a substance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be impelled or driven forward by the action of wind upon sails, as a ship on water; to be impelled on a body of water by steam or other power.","To move through or on the water; to swim, as a fish or a waterfowl."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sail"},{"term":"away","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["From a place, hence.","Aside; off; in another direction."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Away with you! Go away! Begone!"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/away"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sail Away (musical)","blocks":[{"text":"Sail Away is a musical with a book, music and lyrics by Noël Coward. The show was the last musical for which Coward wrote both the book and music, although he wrote the music for one last book musical in 1963."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/57/Sailaway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sail_Away_(musical)"},{"title":"Sail Away (Great White album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sail Away is the seventh studio album by American hard rock band Great White, released in 1994. It was a much mellower effort, dominated by acoustic guitars and laid back performances. Clarence Clemons of the E Street Band plays the sax solo on \"Gone with the Wind\". This is the band's first and only recording with bassist Teddy Cook, as well as their first release for Zoo Entertainment. The original issue came with a bonus CD entitled Anaheim Live. Though these CD's state that the bonus disc was part of a limited edition pressing, no other pressings on CD were made without Anaheim Live, likely because of the poor sales of the album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/SailGW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sail_Away_(Great_White_album)"},{"title":"Sail Away (Randy Newman album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sail Away is the third studio album by American musician Randy Newman, released on May 23, 1972. It was produced by Lenny Waronker and Russ Titelman and issued on Reprise Records. While all of its songs were written and composed by Newman, several had already been recorded by other artists."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0a/Randy_Newman-Sail_Away_%28album_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sail_Away_(Randy_Newman_album)"},{"title":"Sail","blocks":[{"text":"A sail is a tensile structure, which is made from fabric or other membrane materials, that uses wind power to propel sailing craft, including sailing ships, sailboats, windsurfers, ice boats, and even sail-powered land vehicles. Sails may be made from a combination of woven materials—including canvas or polyester cloth, laminated membranes or bonded filaments, usually in a three- or four-sided shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Chesapeake.jpg/330px-Chesapeake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg/500px-Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg/500px-Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg/250px-L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg/250px-L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AL-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg/1280px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Egyptian sailing ship, c. 1422–1411 BCE","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaler_der_Grabkammer_des_Menna_013.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Bgl3t.jpg/500px-Bgl3t.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Bgl3t.jpg/500px-Bgl3t.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A traditional Maldivian Baghlah with a fore-and-aft lateen rig","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABgl3t.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Atlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg/500px-Atlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Atlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg/1280px-Atlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Atlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg/500px-Atlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fijian voyaging outrigger boat with a crab claw sail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtlas_pittoresque_pl_096.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Iranun_Lanong_warship_by_Rafael_Monle%C3%B3n_%281890%29.jpg/500px-Iranun_Lanong_warship_by_Rafael_Monle%C3%B3n_%281890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Iranun_Lanong_warship_by_Rafael_Monle%C3%B3n_%281890%29.jpg/500px-Iranun_Lanong_warship_by_Rafael_Monle%C3%B3n_%281890%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Philippine lanong with tanja sails","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIranun_Lanong_warship_by_Rafael_Monle%C3%B3n_(1890).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Points_of_sail--close-hauled_%28right%29_and_down_wind_%28left%29.jpg/500px-Points_of_sail--close-hauled_%28right%29_and_down_wind_%28left%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Points_of_sail--close-hauled_%28right%29_and_down_wind_%28left%29.jpg/500px-Points_of_sail--close-hauled_%28right%29_and_down_wind_%28left%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerodynamic forces for two points of sail. Left-hand boat:Down wind—predominant drag propels the boat with little heeling moment. Right-hand boat:Up wind (close-hauled)—predominant lift both propels the boat and contributes to heel.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APoints_of_sail--close-hauled_(right)_and_down_wind_(left).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Sail_angles_of_attack_and_resulting_flow_patterns.jpg/500px-Sail_angles_of_attack_and_resulting_flow_patterns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Sail_angles_of_attack_and_resulting_flow_patterns.jpg/500px-Sail_angles_of_attack_and_resulting_flow_patterns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sail angles of attack and resulting (idealized) flow patterns that provide propulsive lift.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASail_angles_of_attack_and_resulting_flow_patterns.jpg"}],"sounds":{"sail":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/En-us-sail.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/46/En-us-sail.ogg/En-us-sail.ogg.mp3"}],"away":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/En-us-away.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/93/En-us-away.ogg/En-us-away.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/46/En-uk-away.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/46/En-uk-away.ogg/En-uk-away.ogg.m